  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "planner-context measures the current session's transcript: the hook passes transcript_path/session_id, context_tokens prefers them, newest-by-mtime stays only as the legacy fallback",
  "spec": "Goal T-1483. Facts (main 355583c): orchestrator/planner_context.py context_tokens(config_dir, root) -> int | None picks max(<config_dir>/projects/<encode_project_dir(root)>/*.jsonl, key=mtime) and returns the last message.usage input+cache_read+cache_creation sum; hook_message(cfg, config_dir, root) formats the handover line when tokens >= [planner].handover_context_tokens. cli.py `planner-context [--hook]` (~609-620) reads CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and calls them. .claude/hooks/planner-prompt.sh runs `uv run orchestrator planner-context --hook` under a 3 s perl alarm and prints its output; it already has the hook stdin in $in, and sibling hooks read `jq -r '.session_id'` from it. Claude Code's UserPromptSubmit stdin carries session_id and transcript_path. Headless decision Planners (planner_runs, `claude -p`, cwd=ROOT) write transcripts into the same projects directory, so the newest file is often not this session's.\n\nChange:\n1. planner_context.context_tokens(config_dir, root, *, transcript=None, session_id=None): resolution order (a) transcript: a Path/str that exists -> use it; (b) session_id: <projects dir>/<session_id>.jsonl when it exists; (c) neither given -> today's newest-by-mtime (legacy, keep so existing callers and tests pass). When (a) or (b) was given but the file does not exist or has no usage line yet (fresh session) -> return None, never fall back to another session's file. Same for hook_message: add the same keyword-only arguments and pass them through.\n2. cli.py planner-context: add `--transcript PATH` and `--session-id ID` options, passed through to both calls.\n3. planner-prompt.sh: `tp=$(jq -r '.transcript_path // \"\"' <<<\"$in\"); sid=$(jq -r '.session_id // \"\"' <<<\"$in\")`, then call `planner-context --hook ${tp:+--transcript \"$tp\"} ${sid:+--session-id \"$sid\"}`; keep the 3 s alarm and fail-open behaviour exactly (no output on any error).\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE): tests/test_planner_context.py::test_context_tokens_from_latest_transcript and test_hook_message_over_threshold call without the new arguments and must pass unchanged (legacy path). New tests in the same file use its fixture style: two transcripts in the projects dir, the older one belonging to the session; with session_id or transcript pointing at it the older file's usage is returned although the other is newer; a session file with no usage returns None (hook_message returns None); a non-existent session_id returns None.\n\nRollback: `git revert` of the merge (hook, CLI and module change together). Out of scope: handover.py, planner_runs.py, pool.toml.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1483. Commit first, then run tests/test_planner_context.py and tests/test_cli.py in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_planner_context.py::test_context_tokens_prefers_session_transcript_over_newest: passes: with two transcripts in the projects dir where the newer one records 190000 context tokens and the older one (named <sid>.jsonl) records 40000, context_tokens(config_dir, root, session_id=sid) == 40000 and context_tokens(config_dir, root, transcript=<older path>) == 40000, while context_tokens(config_dir, root) still returns 190000",
    "tests/test_planner_context.py::test_fresh_session_reports_none_not_another_sessions_size: passes: with a newer 190000-token transcript present, a session transcript that exists but has no usage line, or a session_id with no file, makes context_tokens return None and hook_message return None",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_planner_context_hook_passes_transcript_and_session_id: passes: `orchestrator planner-context --hook --transcript P --session-id S` forwards both to planner_context.hook_message (patched) and prints its return value; without them the call has transcript=None and session_id=None",
    ".claude/hooks/planner-prompt.sh forwards jq '.transcript_path' as --transcript and '.session_id' as --session-id and still exits 0 printing only the mode line when planner-context fails: `echo '{\"prompt\":\"hi\",\"session_id\":\"x\",\"transcript_path\":\"/nonexistent\"}' | .claude/hooks/planner-prompt.sh` prints exactly the 'Planner mode:' line and exits 0",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
